/* The English of this app. The sentence a person reads when the system asks for a permission is written once, in
   Code/Montana/Info.plist: English is the development language, so the phone shows Info.plist's sentence and no line
   here repeats it (constitution article 15, the author's word 18013). Every other language says it in its own
   LANG.lproj/InfoPlist.strings; the Messenger's are written from these by tools/mt-messenger-strings.py. No sentence names
   the app: the system's title above it already does, by the name under the icon (Code/Names.xcconfig). */

/* The name iCloud gives this app's storage (NSUbiquitousContainers in Info.plist). The iCloud
   daemon keeps that name per language and takes each language's name from THIS file only (read
   in its own code, 23.09): without this line the container carried a name in no language at all,
   while Apple's storage page called it "app", the tail of the container's identifier. The
   name is the product's own, Code/Names.xcconfig MT_NAME_PROTOCOL, in every language: tools/mt-owners-check.py holds this
   line equal to it. */
"NSUbiquitousContainerName" = "MT Protocol";
